tes the associated headers. Note that the Twitter domains are still\nimported from Chrome's list of pins, but now have the test flag set, making them inert.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D172161", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/tools/PreloadedHPKPins.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "e26ff04290d095dac006a3710b07077ee5d20f31", "parents": ["d0926aadfbeb06e73068e5ab5b08132b381a7062"], "tags": ["FIREFOX_102_9_0esr_BUILD2", "FIREFOX_102_9_0esr_RELEASE"]}], "date": 1678404381, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}}
